===Etymology 1===
From or related to {{m|rup|fluiarã}}/{{m|rup|fluearã}}. Compare Daco-Romanian {{m|ro|fluiera|fluiera, fluier}}.

===Verb===
{{head|rup|verb|past participle|fluiratã}}

# I [[whistle]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|rup|shuir}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|rup|fluirari}}/{{l|rup|fluirare}}
* {{l|rup|fluirat}}
* {{l|rup|fluiarã}}/{{l|rup|fluearã}}

===Noun===
{{head|rup|noun|g=n}} (''plural'' '''[[fluiri]]'''/'''[[fluire]]''')

# {{alternative form of|fluiarã|lang=rup}}- [[whistle]]

===Etymology 2===
From the above, given the comparison of a bone to a flute; compare Daco-Romanian {{m|ro|fluier}}; cf. also the semantic evolution in Latin {{m|la|tibia}}, which also possessed the sense of "flute".

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|rup|fljer}}, {{l|rup|fler}}, {{l|rup|fljor}}

===Noun===
{{head|rup|noun|g=n}} (''plural'' '''[[fluiri]]'''/'''[[fluire]]''')

# [[tibia]], [[shinbone]]

